  [3mComplexity:[0m moderate, mostly from the dev-workflow change.

  [1mC. Closure inside [38;5;153mapp.js[0m — keep everything in one file; a module-scoped variable plus two functions, no new file.
  [3mWins:[0m smallest possible diff.
  [3mCosts:[0m fails your actual requirement. Other forms on other pages can't reach a closure inside [38;5;153mapp.js[39m without loading
  all of [38;5;153mapp.js[39m, including its [38;5;153m#login-form[39m listener — which throws on any page lacking that form.
  [3mComplexity:[0m trivial, but I'd be building the wrong thing.

  [1mI recommend A.[0m It's the only one that delivers "reachable from other forms" without imposing a build step or a local
  server on a project that currently has neither. B is the better endpoint if this app is going to grow a bundler anyway
  — the honest question is whether it is. C I've listed to rule out.

  Two things I'd fold into A regardless:

  - [1mA [38;5;153mclear()[39m from day one.[0m There's no logout anywhere in the repo, which means nothing would ever remove the id.
    [38;5;153msessionStorage[39m limits the blast radius to the tab, but a store with no eviction path is how stale identity bugs
    start.
  - [1mDefensive storage access.[0m [38;5;153msessionStorage[39m throws in Safari private mode and when storage is disabled. An unguarded
    write in the login path would break login itself for those users — worse than the feature not working.
